1
00:00:00,363 --> 00:00:05,472
The Time Log — Report your work, sick and vacation time — and find, fix and export what you reported.

2
00:00:06,496 --> 00:00:14,100
The Time Log is where you report your time. The form is on the left; everything reported this month is in the table on the right.

3
00:00:14,813 --> 00:00:20,166
The date starts on today. Pick another day in the calendar, or press Today to come back.

4
00:00:20,838 --> 00:00:24,440
The type is Work, Sick or Vacation. We're reporting work.

5
00:00:25,124 --> 00:00:28,977
Set when you started and finished. WorkDesk works out the hours.

6
00:00:32,649 --> 00:00:40,202
Then the hour type. Yellow is client work, billed and drawn from the project's budget. Red is company time. Blue is managing a client's projects.

7
00:00:41,027 --> 00:00:46,635
Choose the client and the project. Not in the list? Type it — a manager verifies it later.

8
00:00:50,158 --> 00:00:55,524
If the work belongs to a work order or one of your Taskana tasks, pick them too.

9
00:00:57,542 --> 00:01:01,462
A short description is required — what did you work on?

10
00:01:07,004 --> 00:01:09,212
Press Add entry.

11
00:01:12,289 --> 00:01:19,331
It's in the table. Its status shows whether it went straight in or is waiting for a manager's approval — over an allowance, for example.

12
00:01:20,027 --> 00:01:23,640
At the end of each row: edit, duplicate and delete.

13
00:01:24,309 --> 00:01:31,418
Duplicate copies the entry to other days in one go — the next day, the rest of the week, or a date you choose.

14
00:01:34,494 --> 00:01:39,003
Pick where it should go. We'll close this for now.

15
00:01:40,213 --> 00:01:47,829
For a day off, set the type to Sick or Vacation. You choose a date range, and WorkDesk counts the working days and shows your balance.

16
00:01:49,877 --> 00:01:54,384
Leave goes to your manager for approval. We'll switch back to Work.

17
00:01:56,895 --> 00:02:03,755
Above the table: move between months, and the totals of what you see — by hour colour, sick days and what's in approval.

18
00:02:04,629 --> 00:02:10,743
Managers can see their team's time too. The filters narrow it down by employee, client, project, work order or status.

19
00:02:11,560 --> 00:02:17,170
This view exports exactly what you see to Excel; Everything exports all the time you're allowed to see.

20
00:02:18,303 --> 00:02:24,682
And every table can be shaped to suit you: save views, sort, move and resize columns — and reset it all.

21
00:02:25,394 --> 00:02:30,077
Report · check · export — Report as you go — it takes a minute a day. More help: the Handbook → Time Log.
